IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc30-forms-register.l4 -- the register of FORM 1 to FORM 23 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46:
-- for each Form, the sections of the Code that the Form's own heading says prescribe it, and the process document the Form prescribes
-- by its own title. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to
-- 2026-09-30); it is not the official text and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- The sections each Form names are PARSED from its heading line by work/gen-register.py, so that a typed number cannot be wrong; the
-- tests (ccc30-tests-forms-register.l4) restate a sample of them by hand from the text.
-- WHAT AN ANSWER MEANS. `forms 1 to 23 the process document the form prescribes` answers a MAYBE: JUST d when the Form's own title is the
-- name of one of the core's process documents; NOTHING when it is not (the core's list has no member for a demand, an order, a report
-- or a committal): the text is silent on whether those are "process documents", which is the keel's word and not the Code's.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `Forms 1 to 23 -- the register`

-- One constructor per Form of lines 17451-18463. Forms 3, 13 and 14 are shown repealed in this text.
DECLARE `forms 1 to 23 which Form` IS ONE OF
    `form 1`
    `form 2`
    `form 3`
    `form 4`
    `form 5`
    `form 5.001`
    `form 5.002`
    `form 5.003`
    `form 5.0031`
    `form 5.0032`
    `form 5.004`
    `form 5.005`
    `form 5.0051`
    `form 5.006`
    `form 5.007`
    `form 5.008`
    `form 5.0081`
    `form 5.009`
    `form 5.0091`
    `form 5.01`
    `form 5.02`
    `form 5.03`
    `form 5.04`
    `form 5.041`
    `form 5.05`
    `form 5.06`
    `form 5.061`
    `form 5.062`
    `form 5.07`
    `form 5.08`
    `form 5.09`
    `form 5.1`
    `form 5.2`
    `form 5.3`
    `form 6`
    `form 6.1`
    `form 6.2`
    `form 6.3`
    `form 6.4`
    `form 7`
    `form 7.1`
    `form 8`
    `form 9`
    `form 10`
    `form 10.1`
    `form 11`
    `form 11.1`
    `form 12`
    `form 13`
    `form 14`
    `form 15`
    `form 16`
    `form 16.1`
    `form 17`
    `form 18`
    `form 19`
    `form 20`
    `form 21`
    `form 22`
    `form 23`

-- A section number as a decimal and a subsection as the Code writes it ("" when the heading names the whole section).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      ss IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Provision of the Code`
`forms 1 to 23 the provision` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF n, ss

-- Form 1: Information To Obtain a Search Warrant
-- src:17451 | FORM 1 (Sections 320.29, 462.32, 462.321 and 487) Information To Obtain a Search Warrant
@ref Form 1 heading (src:17451)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Provision of the Code`
`form 1 the sections that prescribe it` MEANS
    LIST `forms 1 to 23 the provision` 320.29 ""
    , `forms 1 to 23 the provision` 462.32 ""
    , `forms 1 to 23 the provision` 462.321 ""
    , `forms 1 to 23 the provision` 487 ""

